1
00:00:33,036 --> 00:00:34,067
[This drama is fiction.]

2
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:36,223
[Characters, places, events, organization,
and the setting have no connection to reality.]

3
00:00:36,223 --> 00:00:38,151
[Child actors
were filmed under safe conditions.]

4
00:00:47,227 --> 00:00:48,960
Attorney Park Tae Su.

5
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:55,412
Eun Kyung?

6
00:00:58,949 --> 00:01:00,349
Eun Kyung.

7
00:01:05,816 --> 00:01:07,432
Don't you remember me?

8
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,468
Do you know me?

9
00:01:11,051 --> 00:01:13,407
Well, It's been a while.

10
00:01:13,407 --> 00:01:16,267
But you could've at least recognized me.

11
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:21,482
I'll come back later, Attorney Park.

12
00:01:35,178 --> 00:01:37,207
Maybe we can talk tomorrow, then.

13
00:01:48,539 --> 00:01:51,736
You haven't changed, Cha Eun Kyung.

14
00:01:56,926 --> 00:01:59,361
[Episode 2]

15
00:02:08,457 --> 00:02:11,095
What are you doing here?

16
00:02:11,095 --> 00:02:14,390
Didn't Jae Hee say she wanted to stay
a few more nights to spend time with you?

17
00:02:15,719 --> 00:02:18,331
Didn't you tell her to stay
so you could get more work done?

18
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:21,558
You haven't changed at all.
Work always comes first.

19
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,262
Don't assume things.

20
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:28,336
And visitation is part of our agreement,
so please stick to the schedule.

21
00:02:29,876 --> 00:02:32,540
Well, at least Jae Hee has Ji Yoon.

22
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:35,203
They went from friends to sisters.
How nice is that?

23
00:02:36,612 --> 00:02:41,303
Jae Hee has finally gotten used to
you getting remarried.

24
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:44,980
Don't tell me you got any problem.

25
00:02:47,459 --> 00:02:49,435
What are you talking about?

26
00:02:49,435 --> 00:02:51,771
I'm here over a medical malpractice suit.

27
00:02:55,968 --> 00:02:57,368
Bye.

28
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:27,267
Hello.

29
00:03:27,267 --> 00:03:29,633
- I'll head in first.
- Okay.

30
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:36,076
I thought I should explain,
so I came by unannounced.

31
00:03:36,076 --> 00:03:39,386
Oh, Jae Hee explained to me. It's fine.

32
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:41,487
I knew we had an agreement,

33
00:03:41,487 --> 00:03:44,141
but Jae Hee wanted to stay longer. I'm sorry.

34
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:47,811
Her dad had to leave for work early today,
so I came to drop her off.

35
00:03:47,811 --> 00:03:49,479
It's fine.

36
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:53,442
Is everything okay with you?

37
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:55,034
Yes, I'm good, thank you.

38
00:03:58,244 --> 00:03:59,678
Yoo Hee!

39
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:03,886
Thank you for the dumplings.

40
00:04:03,886 --> 00:04:07,013
I heard you made those yourself.
Thank you so much.

41
00:04:07,013 --> 00:04:09,655
My pleasure.
We should both look out for the kids.

42
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,436
Why did Yoo Hee drop you off?

43
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:31,436
Is Dad busy these days?

44
00:04:31,436 --> 00:04:32,520
Yeah.

45
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:34,690
There's some trouble at Dad's hospital.

46
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,111
I'm here over a medical malpractice suit.

47
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:39,454
Why are you asking?

48
00:04:39,454 --> 00:04:41,074
Nothing.

49
00:04:41,074 --> 00:04:42,920
How's the new math academy?

50
00:04:43,927 --> 00:04:45,913
I love it.

51
00:04:45,913 --> 00:04:46,954
That's good.

52
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:48,834
Actually, I want to study somewhere else.

53
00:04:48,834 --> 00:04:50,874
The kid next to me at the library is so loud.

54
00:04:53,025 --> 00:04:56,630
Then how about I set up a study area
for you at home?

55
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,319
- Sounds good.
- Okay.

56
00:05:08,746 --> 00:05:10,964
- See you later.
- Yeah.

57
00:05:10,964 --> 00:05:12,364
See you later!

58
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:21,114
The library?

59
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,631
Could you keep it down, please?

60
00:05:50,631 --> 00:05:52,481
[Law School Library]

61
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:57,707
If it's bothering you so much,
why don't you study at home?

62
00:06:03,697 --> 00:06:05,782
He's still the same, huh?

63
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,528
So annoying.

64
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:15,021
Hey, Kang.

65
00:06:15,021 --> 00:06:18,462
How's the councilor's debt collection going?

66
00:06:18,462 --> 00:06:20,666
Visit the councilor regularly and
keep him updated.

67
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,588
Sir, I'm a lawyer.

68
00:06:26,588 --> 00:06:30,059
You can't keep sending me out
for consultations like this.

69
00:06:30,059 --> 00:06:32,329
That's outdated.
We can't do business like this--

70
00:06:32,329 --> 00:06:35,103
Are you telling me how to run my business?

71
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:36,953
Hey Kang, are you ignoring me?

72
00:06:36,953 --> 00:06:41,079
Think you're big enough to talk back to me?
Then pick one.

73
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:45,231
- Excuse me?
- Do what I say, or quit!

74
00:07:02,174 --> 00:07:05,503
You're Tae Su from By the Law, right?

75
00:07:05,503 --> 00:07:07,803
Wow, you're so handsome!

76
00:07:07,803 --> 00:07:11,974
I watch all your videos! I really love them!

77
00:07:11,974 --> 00:07:13,374
Thank you.

78
00:07:17,563 --> 00:07:20,015
Good morning, Attorney Cha.

79
00:07:23,241 --> 00:07:26,396
You've got a minute? We need to talk.

80
00:07:27,288 --> 00:07:28,688
About what?

81
00:07:35,956 --> 00:07:37,596
After you, Ma'am.

82
00:07:52,064 --> 00:07:54,464
Canned coffee again?

83
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:06,202
We're both going through a hard time,
so let's try to coexist.

84
00:08:13,476 --> 00:08:14,876
You remember!

85
00:08:15,954 --> 00:08:17,821
As you saw earlier,

86
00:08:17,821 --> 00:08:21,168
I'm just as famous as you are now.

87
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:24,208
Use honorifics with me, Attorney Park.

88
00:08:29,593 --> 00:08:32,423
All right, Attorney Cha.

89
00:08:32,423 --> 00:08:36,392
I've got two things to discuss. First...

90
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:40,863
Why was that client here yesterday?

91
00:08:40,863 --> 00:08:42,977
Was it a medical malpractice case?

92
00:08:42,977 --> 00:08:45,832
That's a bit out of line, don't you think?

93
00:08:45,832 --> 00:08:48,725
A lawyer's duty of confidentiality!

94
00:08:50,305 --> 00:08:51,827
And the second one?

95
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,193
Name your price.

96
00:08:55,193 --> 00:08:57,788
How much to get you off the eighth floor?

97
00:08:57,788 --> 00:09:01,012
I'll pay handsomely. Please leave.

98
00:09:01,012 --> 00:09:03,085
Now that's pretty out of line.

99
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:07,076
What'll it take to get you out?

100
00:09:07,076 --> 00:09:09,054
I want the seventh floor, too.

101
00:09:09,675 --> 00:09:14,038
Go ahead and try. Everyone will still see
this place as part of REBOM.

102
00:09:14,038 --> 00:09:16,639
I've been here for over two years.

103
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:20,185
Then from now on,
everyone will know this place as TAESU.

104
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:22,376
I'm going to stay here for 20 years.

105
00:09:22,376 --> 00:09:24,258
Then I guess we're done.

106
00:09:33,985 --> 00:09:35,841
[Congratulations, Cha Eun Kyung!
Top Scorer on the 46th Bar Exam in Record Time]

107
00:09:39,037 --> 00:09:40,983
I passed early, thanks to you.

108
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,427
You were so noisy, I couldn't stand it.

109
00:09:45,394 --> 00:09:46,794
Bye.

110
00:09:51,831 --> 00:09:55,497
Still the same.
You say your piece and just walk away.

111
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:03,579
You'll see. You'll be the one leaving.

112
00:10:03,579 --> 00:10:04,959
[Attorney Jeon Eun Ho]

113
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:13,238
Hello, this is Attorney Jeon.
We spoke last week.

114
00:10:14,489 --> 00:10:17,879
Oh, I see... You signed with another firm.

115
00:10:19,661 --> 00:10:22,623
TAESU Law Firm?

116
00:10:22,623 --> 00:10:25,690
All right. Thank you.

117
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:35,435
It's annoying. Really annoying.

118
00:10:39,331 --> 00:10:41,102
[TAESU Law Firm, Senior Partner Park Tae Su]

119
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,522
[Your Strongest Sword and Shield]

120
00:11:21,465 --> 00:11:24,768
Ma'am, do you know Attorney Park?

121
00:11:24,768 --> 00:11:28,229
We went to college together.
He's such a copycat.

122
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:31,140
When he was studying for the bar,
he even got the same pen and notebook as me.

123
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:35,833
So the guy paying double rent
for the eighth floor is Attorney Park,

124
00:11:35,833 --> 00:11:39,268
and you two went to the same college?

125
00:11:39,268 --> 00:11:41,974
Wow, Small world!

126
00:11:45,828 --> 00:11:51,378
Ma'am, Attorney Park only got a little
attention because the algorithm picked him.

127
00:11:51,378 --> 00:11:53,880
But you're the one clients pick.

128
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:59,093
Beautiful, smart,
a real professional lawyer. Got it?

129
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,257
Very convincing. You're a lawyer, after all.

130
00:12:01,257 --> 00:12:02,284
Thank you.

131
00:12:02,284 --> 00:12:05,791
Let's see how long he lasts.

132
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:08,394
With rent this high,
paying double is ridiculous.

133
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:10,933
I know. It's like a war in here.

134
00:12:10,933 --> 00:12:15,473
But if we're going to strengthen our forces
in this war,

135
00:12:15,473 --> 00:12:20,616
I think we need another lawyer.
What do you think?

136
00:12:20,616 --> 00:12:23,595
- I was just about to tell you.
- Yes.

137
00:12:23,595 --> 00:12:26,738
- I think I found one.
- No way! No way!

138
00:12:26,738 --> 00:12:29,709
You said a new hire was coming,
but no one ever showed up.

139
00:12:29,709 --> 00:12:31,322
I'm pretty sure this time.

140
00:12:32,144 --> 00:12:33,544
Who is it?

141
00:12:37,414 --> 00:12:39,119
Kang Hye Seong.

142
00:12:39,119 --> 00:12:40,296
What?

143
00:12:40,296 --> 00:12:41,636
She never gives up.

144
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:46,016
She fights to the end
for what's best for her clients.

145
00:12:46,016 --> 00:12:48,060
I haven't seen a lawyer like that in ages.

146
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:51,605
- I told you that when we were having lunch.
- Exactly!

147
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:56,860
I'll find out if she's interested in
divorce cases and open to switching firms.

148
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,480
Need to find the right timing.

149
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:03,569
[Case 02: Timing]
Should I call her first?

150
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:12,405
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm's Problem Solver,
Attorney Kang Hye Seong]

151
00:13:21,466 --> 00:13:24,680
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm]
Councilor, did you see Attorney Kang sing?

152
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,515
- I'm sorry.
- What the...

153
00:13:26,515 --> 00:13:32,255
She's good at everything. Drinking,
civil cases, criminal cases, you name it.

154
00:13:32,255 --> 00:13:34,850
Don't worry.

155
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:38,272
She's a nobody.
She has to do whatever I tell her.

156
00:13:38,272 --> 00:13:41,401
Then I'll see you tonight. Thank you.

157
00:13:41,401 --> 00:13:42,585
Yes.

158
00:13:44,656 --> 00:13:46,622
What is this, the '80s?

159
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:52,607
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm]

160
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:03,468
Can I meet Attorney Kang?

161
00:14:03,468 --> 00:14:06,195
Her schedule is completely booked today.

162
00:14:06,195 --> 00:14:09,442
If you don't have an appointment,
you'll have to wait in line.

163
00:14:11,614 --> 00:14:13,014
Okay.

164
00:14:36,335 --> 00:14:39,379
There's an empty seat. Would you like to move?

165
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:41,307
- Sure.
- Yes.

166
00:15:05,531 --> 00:15:09,764
Does she really handle
all these consultations by herself?

167
00:15:10,369 --> 00:15:12,871
I'm here for a consultation.

168
00:15:12,871 --> 00:15:15,336
Please have a seat and wait a moment.

169
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:26,741
Could you give this to Attorney Kang?

170
00:15:26,741 --> 00:15:29,141
- Please ask her to call me.
- Sure.

171
00:15:35,268 --> 00:15:37,807
She's really busy. You can't just--

172
00:15:37,807 --> 00:15:39,132
[Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

173
00:15:42,726 --> 00:15:44,913
Cha Eun Kyung...

174
00:15:49,285 --> 00:15:53,115
We've been married for five years,
and we don't have kids.

175
00:15:53,996 --> 00:15:55,878
Please help me get a divorce.

176
00:15:55,878 --> 00:15:57,851
What's the reason?

177
00:15:58,834 --> 00:16:00,620
He goes gambling.

178
00:16:10,572 --> 00:16:12,347
[Cheonghae Zone Game Center
The best odds in town!]

179
00:16:12,347 --> 00:16:17,804
He took about 500 million won
from his father and lost it.

180
00:16:19,813 --> 00:16:22,843
I told you!
One more time, and I'm divorcing you!

181
00:16:25,091 --> 00:16:29,424
When I told him to stop gambling, he hit me.

182
00:16:33,825 --> 00:16:36,830
I said I wouldn't do it!

183
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:38,470
I said I wouldn't!

184
00:16:44,379 --> 00:16:46,215
Get over here.

185
00:16:46,215 --> 00:16:47,695
Get over here!

186
00:16:53,347 --> 00:16:56,820
- Stop it!
- Stay still!

187
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:59,054
Just stay still!

188
00:17:00,588 --> 00:17:04,309
There. That's better.

189
00:17:14,503 --> 00:17:19,498
Every time I brought up divorce,
he'd sign a written promise not to do it again.

190
00:17:19,498 --> 00:17:21,791
And then it happened all over again.

191
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:23,448
[Emergency Room]

192
00:17:23,448 --> 00:17:28,614
He only signed it because his parents would
disinherit him if we divorced.

193
00:17:30,884 --> 00:17:35,754
But there were more than gambling and abuse.

194
00:17:39,518 --> 00:17:41,124
There was another woman?

195
00:17:42,539 --> 00:17:44,767
Another woman would be better.

196
00:17:45,524 --> 00:17:49,152
Gosh, I've been waiting forever.

197
00:17:49,152 --> 00:17:50,462
Was he having an affair with a man?

198
00:17:50,462 --> 00:17:52,155
You weren't waiting for me.

199
00:17:52,155 --> 00:17:54,496
You were waiting for this, right?

200
00:17:54,496 --> 00:17:57,237
You are the best!

201
00:18:02,374 --> 00:18:03,774
Drugs.

202
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,206
Gambling, abuse, and drugs...

203
00:18:12,206 --> 00:18:14,965
That's more than enough grounds for divorce.

204
00:18:14,965 --> 00:18:16,736
What do you want to do?

205
00:18:21,464 --> 00:18:25,606
I want to make him pay. As much as possible.

206
00:18:25,606 --> 00:18:30,064
Why just make him pay?
We should crush him completely!

207
00:18:30,064 --> 00:18:31,464
How?

208
00:18:35,188 --> 00:18:40,289
"Criminal Charges," "Property Division,"
"Property Seizure," and "Restraining Order."

209
00:18:40,996 --> 00:18:43,575
Let's file all four at once.

210
00:18:44,666 --> 00:18:46,542
Should we start with the Criminal complaint?

211
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,893
We can't file a criminal complaint yet.

212
00:18:48,893 --> 00:18:51,710
For now, let's just file for divorce mediation.

213
00:18:51,710 --> 00:18:55,531
Why? We should go after property division
and file criminal charges, too!

214
00:18:55,531 --> 00:18:58,877
The attorney upstairs told me to file all four.

215
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:08,116
Most of your husband's
three billion won in assets was gifted to him.

216
00:19:08,116 --> 00:19:11,577
You've only been married for five years
and have no kids.

217
00:19:11,577 --> 00:19:14,271
You probably won't get much
in the property division.

218
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:25,018
He has three billion won,
and his parents have tens of billions.

219
00:19:25,018 --> 00:19:27,044
Because of him, I've...

220
00:19:28,627 --> 00:19:33,966
had to take antidepressants,
and I can't live a normal life. But he is...

221
00:19:33,966 --> 00:19:37,083
That's why we shouldn't sue right now.

222
00:19:37,083 --> 00:19:40,443
His parents are wealthy, not your husband.

223
00:19:40,443 --> 00:19:43,464
If his assets are deemed separate property,
splitting them won't be easy.

224
00:19:43,464 --> 00:19:45,528
And compensation won't be much.

225
00:19:45,528 --> 00:19:49,126
You may not understand
what I'm saying right now.

226
00:19:49,126 --> 00:19:52,141
But if you want some compensation for
what you've been through,

227
00:19:52,141 --> 00:19:56,196
mediation is a better option
than going to trial.

228
00:19:56,196 --> 00:19:59,371
Just watch how I handle this.

229
00:20:20,504 --> 00:20:22,831
[Hyeseong's Bunsik]

230
00:20:24,102 --> 00:20:27,224
Do what I say, or quit!

231
00:20:27,224 --> 00:20:30,975
But I know everyone in Gwangjin.
Do you really think you can practice law here?

232
00:20:30,975 --> 00:20:33,851
Besides, because of your dad,
you're stuck in Gwangjin anyway, right?

233
00:20:42,242 --> 00:20:44,203
Dad!

234
00:20:44,203 --> 00:20:46,004
Hey, sweetie. You're home.

235
00:20:46,004 --> 00:20:47,404
Let me carry that.

236
00:21:10,608 --> 00:21:14,094
Dad, should I sell tteokbokki with you?

237
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:16,300
What?

238
00:21:17,444 --> 00:21:20,572
Don't be ridiculous.

239
00:21:20,572 --> 00:21:22,156
Who knows?

240
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:25,964
I might make more money than I do as a lawyer.

241
00:21:25,964 --> 00:21:29,297
Besides, AI's going to replace
knowledge workers soon anyway.

242
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:33,006
Making more money isn't what matters.

243
00:21:33,006 --> 00:21:34,548
Of course it is.

244
00:21:34,548 --> 00:21:39,340
You worked so hard paying off
my law school loans.

245
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,526
Don't make money your priority.

246
00:21:41,526 --> 00:21:44,546
You wanted to be a lawyer so badly.

247
00:21:48,951 --> 00:21:54,308
Dad, do you know why I wanted to become
a lawyer in the first place?

248
00:21:55,399 --> 00:21:57,915
Don't tell me it was to make a lot of money.

249
00:21:57,915 --> 00:22:00,283
Gosh, you're impossible!

250
00:22:09,730 --> 00:22:12,138
Did the surgery go well?

251
00:22:12,138 --> 00:22:18,094
[Five years ago]
Yes, but I'm not sure he can walk again.

252
00:22:18,094 --> 00:22:20,534
[Operating Room]
He needs help from his family.

253
00:22:30,488 --> 00:22:32,937
[Congratulations on joining DAEJEONG Law Firm]

254
00:22:41,069 --> 00:22:43,629
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

255
00:22:49,955 --> 00:22:53,579
All right.
We'll look for another attorney then.

256
00:22:53,579 --> 00:22:57,268
Hope your father makes a full recovery.

257
00:22:58,792 --> 00:23:02,550
Dad, you must be sick of hospital food.
I'll make you something nice.

258
00:23:26,410 --> 00:23:27,810
Yes.

259
00:23:29,249 --> 00:23:34,267
Ma'am, you went all the way to
Gwangjin yourself? I could've gone.

260
00:23:34,267 --> 00:23:35,985
I wanted to talk to her in person.

261
00:23:35,985 --> 00:23:38,846
What did Attorney Kang say? Can she move?

262
00:23:38,846 --> 00:23:41,713
Is she a fan of yours?
Can she start right away?

263
00:23:41,713 --> 00:23:43,047
I didn't get to meet her.

264
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:45,560
You went all that way and didn't meet her?

265
00:23:47,217 --> 00:23:49,261
There were so many people
waiting for consultations.

266
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,971
The firm had no specialty and handled
a high volume of cases for low fees.

267
00:23:51,971 --> 00:23:54,943
It was more like a public service desk
than a law firm.

268
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:58,354
And the senior partner seems awful.

269
00:23:58,354 --> 00:24:01,411
It might be a perfect time to recruit her,
but...

270
00:24:01,411 --> 00:24:03,668
The timing does seem right,

271
00:24:03,668 --> 00:24:06,445
but she'd have to give up her entire career
in civil and criminal law

272
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:08,715
and start from scratch in divorce law.

273
00:24:08,715 --> 00:24:10,715
That's what worries you, right?

274
00:24:10,715 --> 00:24:13,278
Exactly! You catch on fast.

275
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:20,052
Criminal Case No. 201-5423 is now in session.

276
00:24:20,052 --> 00:24:22,757
Prosecution, please state the charges.

277
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:27,373
On March 3, 2026, at around 8 p.m.,

278
00:24:27,373 --> 00:24:30,340
The defendant entered her ex-boyfriend's home
without permission by entering the door code.

279
00:24:30,340 --> 00:24:34,699
She trespassed into his home,
disturbing his peace and privacy.

280
00:24:34,699 --> 00:24:39,972
Therefore, the defendant violated Article 319,
Paragraph 1 of the Criminal Act.

281
00:24:39,972 --> 00:24:42,239
Defense, go ahead.

282
00:24:45,904 --> 00:24:48,310
I plead not guilty.

283
00:24:50,408 --> 00:24:54,090
- She looks like a rookie, pleading not guilty?
- Your Honor.

284
00:24:54,090 --> 00:24:59,957
To prove trespassing, you must show that
she intended to disturb the peace of his home.

285
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:06,170
But my client wasn't trespassing.
She was just trying to win back her ex.

286
00:25:06,170 --> 00:25:12,336
How can someone be an intruder
after eight years of coming and going freely?

287
00:25:12,336 --> 00:25:15,940
The defendant made a terrible mistake,
and what she did was wrong.

288
00:25:15,940 --> 00:25:19,182
But under the Criminal Act, she's not guilty!

289
00:25:20,062 --> 00:25:22,662
Oh, she's pretty good.

290
00:25:44,739 --> 00:25:47,149
Thank you for trusting REBOM with your case.

291
00:25:47,149 --> 00:25:51,352
But why do lawyers give such different advice?

292
00:25:52,009 --> 00:25:54,322
Well, everyone sees things differently.

293
00:25:54,322 --> 00:25:59,558
A judge's ruling and a lawyer's advice
won't always be the same.

294
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:01,192
Just trust me.

295
00:26:01,192 --> 00:26:02,876
Hello. Good morning.

296
00:26:02,876 --> 00:26:05,360
Good morning.

297
00:26:07,306 --> 00:26:08,751
Attorney Kang,

298
00:26:09,715 --> 00:26:13,740
I couldn't tell you yesterday
with the senior partner around, but guess what?

299
00:26:14,693 --> 00:26:17,230
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung stopped by.

300
00:26:19,676 --> 00:26:21,379
Why?

301
00:26:21,379 --> 00:26:24,204
Maybe she came to recruit you.

302
00:26:25,726 --> 00:26:27,745
[REBOM Law Firm
Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

303
00:26:30,599 --> 00:26:31,632
[Central Family Court]

304
00:26:31,632 --> 00:26:34,879
The petition doesn't go into much detail.

305
00:26:34,879 --> 00:26:36,924
What's your reason for divorce?

306
00:26:36,924 --> 00:26:40,156
[Plaintiff's Table]
Well, the reason is... d...

307
00:26:45,521 --> 00:26:48,024
Let's just say... deep emotional distress.

308
00:26:48,024 --> 00:26:51,091
[Defendant's Table]
Yes.

309
00:26:51,091 --> 00:26:55,970
Respondent has approximately
three billion won in assets. Is that correct?

310
00:26:55,970 --> 00:27:00,338
That's right. But most of his assets
were gifted from his parents.

311
00:27:00,338 --> 00:27:02,354
They're not subject to division.

312
00:27:02,354 --> 00:27:04,369
Okay, but we're here for mediation, so...

313
00:27:04,369 --> 00:27:08,441
How much would you be willing to pay
the applicant in a divorce?

314
00:27:08,441 --> 00:27:10,631
Well, as a goodwill gesture...

315
00:27:10,631 --> 00:27:13,638
He'd be willing to pay around 20 million won.

316
00:27:14,256 --> 00:27:16,183
20 million? You've got to be kidding me.

317
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:20,943
We haven't taken any other legal action

318
00:27:20,943 --> 00:27:23,644
because we wanted to settle things amicably
as a goodwill gesture.

319
00:27:23,644 --> 00:27:27,136
But it seems we have very different ideas
about what a goodwill gesture means.

320
00:27:27,969 --> 00:27:30,065
20 million won is the most we can offer.

321
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:31,618
Let's just settle for 20 million won.

322
00:27:31,618 --> 00:27:33,740
Then let's take it to court.

323
00:27:33,740 --> 00:27:35,147
Fine.

324
00:27:35,147 --> 00:27:39,160
- Maybe you should hear their offer--
- There's nothing to hear!

325
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:41,614
Let's go to trial!

326
00:27:50,864 --> 00:27:52,693
Attorney Cha!

327
00:27:53,703 --> 00:27:55,796
Please wait over there.

328
00:27:58,983 --> 00:28:01,013
You're blackmailing us, not negotiating.

329
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:03,278
It's not blackmail. It's a deal.

330
00:28:03,278 --> 00:28:04,933
That's what we do.

331
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:07,880
Each side gives a little to find common ground.

332
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:12,007
Are you saying you'll file criminal charges
if we can't reach a settlement?

333
00:28:14,199 --> 00:28:16,129
Are you going to report him for using drugs?

334
00:28:16,129 --> 00:28:18,374
You got my point.

335
00:28:18,374 --> 00:28:23,770
Assault, rape, and drug use. All three charges.

336
00:28:23,770 --> 00:28:27,753
How can we trust that you won't file charges
if we settle?

337
00:28:27,753 --> 00:28:31,029
Believe us or not, that's your problem.

338
00:28:31,029 --> 00:28:34,630
Put the house he's living in in her name,
and we'll drop the whole thing.

339
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:36,451
We'll even sign a confidentiality agreement.

340
00:28:36,451 --> 00:28:37,790
Have you lost your mind?

341
00:28:37,790 --> 00:28:40,512
That house is worth two billion won!

342
00:28:40,512 --> 00:28:43,934
How can a housewife who sits around all day
get a house worth two billion won?

343
00:28:43,934 --> 00:28:47,721
Even lawyers who've worked 20 years
can't afford a house like that these days!

344
00:28:47,721 --> 00:28:49,647
You still haven't bought one?

345
00:28:49,647 --> 00:28:52,765
Then maybe you should stay home, too.

346
00:28:52,765 --> 00:28:55,882
That's my final offer.
Think it over and call me.

347
00:28:58,530 --> 00:29:02,293
Attorney Cha, I've been thinking...

348
00:29:03,287 --> 00:29:06,087
I'd be fine with just 180 million won.

349
00:29:06,899 --> 00:29:11,631
180 million? How'd you come up with that?

350
00:29:11,631 --> 00:29:17,090
3 million a month, 12 months a year,
for 5 years.

351
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:19,801
Just sign the divorce papers, please.

352
00:29:19,801 --> 00:29:21,955
- Please...
- Get off me!

353
00:29:24,431 --> 00:29:29,523
I don't need money. Just please let me go!

354
00:29:30,747 --> 00:29:31,954
Hey.

355
00:29:31,954 --> 00:29:34,826
Do you know how much it costs
to hire a housekeeper?

356
00:29:34,826 --> 00:29:38,605
I should pay at least three million won
a month. Am I crazy?

357
00:29:40,030 --> 00:29:42,310
Shut up and clean my house.

358
00:29:42,950 --> 00:29:46,245
He treated me like his housekeeper,

359
00:29:46,245 --> 00:29:48,365
so I want at least that much.

360
00:29:50,624 --> 00:29:53,126
Then you're doing the math wrong.

361
00:29:54,418 --> 00:29:55,477
What?

362
00:29:55,477 --> 00:29:58,924
Abuse, assault, rape, drugs...

363
00:29:58,924 --> 00:30:01,552
You'll be scarred for life.

364
00:30:01,552 --> 00:30:05,127
You're only counting what you've done so far.
What about compensation for

365
00:30:05,127 --> 00:30:07,078
the emotional damage you'll suffer
in the future?

366
00:30:07,705 --> 00:30:10,884
2 billion won is worth fighting for.
Don't back down.

367
00:30:11,562 --> 00:30:16,314
But if he pays,
we'll let everything he's done go.

368
00:30:16,314 --> 00:30:20,422
You're getting a lot of money in exchange for
keeping his big secret.

369
00:30:20,422 --> 00:30:22,880
You understand that's the deal, right?

370
00:30:26,660 --> 00:30:28,141
Yes.

371
00:30:40,613 --> 00:30:44,261
The defendant made a terrible mistake,
and what she did was wrong.

372
00:30:44,261 --> 00:30:47,526
But under the Criminal Act, she's not guilty!

373
00:30:53,605 --> 00:30:55,258
[Gwangjin District Court: Case Number]

374
00:30:57,337 --> 00:30:58,722
[Case Search]

375
00:30:58,722 --> 00:31:01,028
[Verdict: Not Guilty, April 19, 2026]

376
00:31:01,028 --> 00:31:02,428
Not guilty?

377
00:31:04,019 --> 00:31:06,074
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm, Attorney: Kang Hye Seong]
What?

378
00:31:06,074 --> 00:31:08,074
She really made it?

379
00:31:16,215 --> 00:31:18,376
[REBOM Law Firm: Interview Schedule]

380
00:31:23,441 --> 00:31:27,751
Hello. Please come this way.

381
00:31:27,751 --> 00:31:29,883
[REBOM Law Firm]

382
00:31:36,313 --> 00:31:39,223
Hello. Are you Attorney Kang Hye Seong?

383
00:31:39,223 --> 00:31:40,931
Right this way, please.

384
00:31:53,675 --> 00:31:57,584
- You're here?
- Hello, Attorney Cha. Nice to see you again.

385
00:31:57,584 --> 00:31:58,984
Have a seat.

386
00:32:01,964 --> 00:32:05,761
You know we're a divorce law firm, right?

387
00:32:05,761 --> 00:32:07,702
Yes, I do.

388
00:32:08,512 --> 00:32:12,155
Any questions about us before we begin?

389
00:32:13,997 --> 00:32:17,936
May I ask why you decided to interview me?

390
00:32:18,979 --> 00:32:21,296
Whether you believed your client or not,

391
00:32:21,296 --> 00:32:25,443
you stood by your client and defended them
to the very end.

392
00:32:25,443 --> 00:32:27,450
Your Honor, the agreement never says

393
00:32:27,450 --> 00:32:32,375
the plaintiff threatened or
coerced her to meet other men.

394
00:32:32,375 --> 00:32:35,787
And you went out of your way to find evidence
and bring it to court.

395
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:39,070
These are market price reports for the condo
from ten realtors.

396
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:42,128
That's the kind of sincerity and dedication
I was looking for.

397
00:32:44,047 --> 00:32:47,155
But I still lost the case.

398
00:32:48,218 --> 00:32:53,943
It's rare to find a lawyer who truly believes
in their client and fights for them these days.

399
00:32:55,141 --> 00:32:57,113
Thank you.

400
00:32:57,113 --> 00:33:02,692
But to be honest, I have very little experience
with divorce cases.

401
00:33:02,692 --> 00:33:05,025
I thought I could handle them,

402
00:33:05,025 --> 00:33:07,685
but they're very different
from civil and criminal cases.

403
00:33:07,685 --> 00:33:09,781
Is she here to turn down the offer?

404
00:33:09,781 --> 00:33:11,742
That's right.

405
00:33:11,742 --> 00:33:17,921
Divorce cases are different. It's like...

406
00:33:17,921 --> 00:33:20,580
It's like an art in itself.

407
00:33:26,712 --> 00:33:31,874
If you join us, I'll offer you
the highest salary for someone at your level.

408
00:33:32,930 --> 00:33:36,193
Do you need some time to think it over?

409
00:33:37,851 --> 00:33:40,938
Yes. Thank you for the offer.

410
00:33:40,938 --> 00:33:43,082
I'll think it over.

411
00:33:52,039 --> 00:33:53,738
Attorney Kang?

412
00:33:56,088 --> 00:33:59,829
Oh, you know me?
I'm a subscriber to By the Law!

413
00:33:59,829 --> 00:34:01,331
Really?

414
00:34:01,331 --> 00:34:04,187
I was just about to become a fan of yours, too.

415
00:34:04,187 --> 00:34:07,714
- Sorry?
- I saw you plead not guilty in court.

416
00:34:07,714 --> 00:34:09,810
And you actually got your client acquitted.

417
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:13,308
An acquittal just five years into your career.
That's impressive!

418
00:34:13,308 --> 00:34:17,126
You really do know me. Thank you.

419
00:34:17,891 --> 00:34:19,983
What brings you here?

420
00:34:19,983 --> 00:34:24,129
I'm here for an interview.
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung invited me.

421
00:34:26,205 --> 00:34:28,819
[TAESU Law Firm, REBOM Law Firm]
You're fast, Cha Eun Kyung.

422
00:34:28,819 --> 00:34:32,092
So she's worth hiring, even from Gwangjin?

423
00:34:33,153 --> 00:34:36,326
Since you're in Seoul, how about having tea?

424
00:34:36,326 --> 00:34:39,740
I'd like to chat with one of my subscribers.

425
00:34:41,301 --> 00:34:45,919
[TAESU Law Firm]

426
00:34:45,919 --> 00:34:48,261
I already know you're good in court.

427
00:34:49,024 --> 00:34:51,341
Have you brought in clients yourself?

428
00:34:51,341 --> 00:34:54,150
Yes! Our firm is small,

429
00:34:54,150 --> 00:34:57,151
so I handle consultations,
take on cases, go to court,

430
00:34:57,151 --> 00:34:59,710
and even collect success fees all by myself.

431
00:35:01,752 --> 00:35:03,152
What do you specialize in?

432
00:35:04,249 --> 00:35:06,313
That's not common in small cities.

433
00:35:06,313 --> 00:35:09,525
I've handled civil, criminal,
administrative, and divorce cases.

434
00:35:09,525 --> 00:35:13,739
I've handled a lot of small claims cases
in particular.

435
00:35:13,739 --> 00:35:16,283
You're literally good at everything, huh?

436
00:35:16,283 --> 00:35:20,229
Then you must get a lot of bonuses.

437
00:35:21,104 --> 00:35:24,249
No, I just get a salary.

438
00:35:24,249 --> 00:35:28,377
Our firm is small, so even though we have
a lot of cases, we don't make much.

439
00:35:28,377 --> 00:35:29,792
That's ridiculous!

440
00:35:29,792 --> 00:35:32,041
Why bring in clients
if they're not paying you more?

441
00:35:32,041 --> 00:35:33,710
Just to make the senior partner richer?

442
00:35:34,801 --> 00:35:36,852
I wanted to learn along the way.

443
00:35:36,852 --> 00:35:40,605
I thought that would help me move on
to the next step in my career.

444
00:35:46,114 --> 00:35:51,059
Then how about making TAESU your next step?

445
00:35:51,775 --> 00:35:55,982
I'll offer you a better deal than
Attorney Cha did.

446
00:35:55,982 --> 00:35:57,382
Excuse me?

447
00:35:59,535 --> 00:36:02,585
We handle just about every kind of case.

448
00:36:02,585 --> 00:36:04,998
You seem like a criminal lawyer to me.

449
00:36:04,998 --> 00:36:09,878
You can't just throw away five years of
experience in civil and criminal law.

450
00:36:11,296 --> 00:36:14,129
Thank you for the offer, but...

451
00:36:16,093 --> 00:36:19,462
Timing is everything!

452
00:36:36,358 --> 00:36:38,085
Hello, Ma'am.

453
00:36:39,717 --> 00:36:41,535
You're here, Ma'am.

454
00:36:41,535 --> 00:36:44,859
Should I reach out to Attorney Kang for you?

455
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:49,520
She said she has some personal issues
to deal with.

456
00:36:49,520 --> 00:36:51,320
Give her some time.

457
00:36:51,320 --> 00:36:52,720
- Yes.
- Okay.

458
00:37:02,449 --> 00:37:03,962
Hey, Kang!

459
00:37:06,099 --> 00:37:07,467
There you are!

460
00:37:07,467 --> 00:37:11,090
One of my friends in Seoul
told me something strange.

461
00:37:11,090 --> 00:37:13,647
Why did you meet Cha Eun Kyung
when the trial was already over?

462
00:37:14,983 --> 00:37:16,029
- Why?
- Well...

463
00:37:16,029 --> 00:37:18,718
To get you to join her firm? Right?

464
00:37:21,275 --> 00:37:26,895
- Yes, but I...
- Think you'll make it in Seoul like she did?

465
00:37:28,288 --> 00:37:32,384
Without me, you're only half as good a lawyer.
You're just handling routine cases.

466
00:37:32,384 --> 00:37:33,427
Got it?

467
00:37:36,743 --> 00:37:39,918
What? You want to hit me?

468
00:37:39,918 --> 00:37:43,981
You're just using your dad as an excuse
not to go to Seoul, aren't you?

469
00:37:43,981 --> 00:37:48,384
You really think your dad can afford to open
a firm for you just by selling tteokbokki?

470
00:37:48,384 --> 00:37:51,451
Oh, please. Know your place.

471
00:37:54,547 --> 00:37:59,952
I've recorded everything you've said to me,
including today.

472
00:37:59,952 --> 00:38:03,012
I'll consider how to use this as a lawyer.

473
00:38:04,981 --> 00:38:07,866
Are you threatening me?
Is that what I taught you?

474
00:38:07,866 --> 00:38:10,513
Did you ever teach me anything?

475
00:38:11,748 --> 00:38:13,554
I'm quitting.

476
00:38:13,554 --> 00:38:15,420
Send my things to me.

477
00:38:15,420 --> 00:38:16,713
Hey!

478
00:38:16,713 --> 00:38:19,046
Hey, Kang!

479
00:38:20,217 --> 00:38:22,499
Hey! I'm not finished yet!

480
00:38:41,340 --> 00:38:43,375
[Attorney Park Tae Su]

481
00:38:48,546 --> 00:38:50,411
Hello, Attorney Park.

482
00:38:50,411 --> 00:38:54,052
Attorney Kang, have you made up your mind?

483
00:38:54,052 --> 00:38:56,405
You've kept me waiting so long.

484
00:38:59,342 --> 00:39:03,092
Attorney Park, can we meet tomorrow?

485
00:39:03,092 --> 00:39:04,705
Sure!

486
00:39:06,288 --> 00:39:07,568
Yes.

487
00:39:10,559 --> 00:39:14,974
I knew she couldn't turn down my offer!

488
00:39:17,552 --> 00:39:22,237
Attorney Cha, I'm getting really worried.
They still haven't called me.

489
00:39:22,237 --> 00:39:24,823
It's all about timing
when it comes to settlement.

490
00:39:24,823 --> 00:39:27,159
Just wait a bit more.

491
00:39:27,159 --> 00:39:30,684
Should I call the police right now?

492
00:39:30,684 --> 00:39:34,597
If I don't report him,
someone else could get hurt.

493
00:39:34,597 --> 00:39:39,379
Are you considering the public interest
while you're getting divorced?

494
00:39:39,379 --> 00:39:42,341
Just think about what's best for you.

495
00:39:42,341 --> 00:39:47,566
He'll probably start getting nervous
and offering more money by now.

496
00:39:48,166 --> 00:39:52,344
And make sure you leave the house.
It's dangerous.

497
00:39:53,956 --> 00:39:55,270
So...

498
00:39:55,270 --> 00:39:59,691
I told you to raise the offer
to around 100 million won!

499
00:39:59,691 --> 00:40:01,985
100 million?
They're asking for two billion won!

500
00:40:01,985 --> 00:40:06,121
They won't even take that seriously.
Let's just go to trial!

501
00:40:08,825 --> 00:40:12,758
So you're telling me to save my money
and just go to prison?

502
00:40:12,758 --> 00:40:17,500
I'm telling you to pick one.
Pay more or go to prison!

503
00:40:19,753 --> 00:40:21,303
Hello? Hel--

504
00:40:22,189 --> 00:40:25,999
What is wrong with him?

505
00:40:29,239 --> 00:40:30,719
What the...

506
00:40:32,432 --> 00:40:36,248
So you've decided? When can you start?

507
00:40:38,032 --> 00:40:42,062
Before I decide, I'd like to ask one thing.

508
00:40:43,458 --> 00:40:47,100
What role do you expect me to take on
at the firm?

509
00:40:48,574 --> 00:40:54,361
She wants to know where she fits in?
That means she wants to be useful.

510
00:40:54,361 --> 00:40:56,467
Oh, I want her even more.

511
00:40:58,709 --> 00:41:03,241
You have plenty of experience
in both civil and criminal cases.

512
00:41:03,241 --> 00:41:06,721
I can put you on any team you prefer,

513
00:41:07,501 --> 00:41:12,526
but to sell the "Attorney Kang Gets Acquittals"
image, the criminal team is a better fit.

514
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:22,173
I'm sorry I can't give you an answer
right away.

515
00:41:22,173 --> 00:41:26,192
Once I choose a firm, I tend to stay
for a long time.

516
00:41:26,192 --> 00:41:28,052
Playing hard to get, huh?

517
00:41:28,763 --> 00:41:30,996
So I'm the one being interviewed now?

518
00:41:32,395 --> 00:41:34,468
Not at all!

519
00:41:34,468 --> 00:41:38,007
I can give you more time.

520
00:41:38,007 --> 00:41:40,061
Thank you.

521
00:41:53,019 --> 00:41:54,662
[REBOM Law Firm]

522
00:41:58,564 --> 00:42:01,943
[Attorney Cha Eun Kyung]

523
00:42:06,031 --> 00:42:07,755
[Boss]

524
00:42:09,683 --> 00:42:12,074
Hey! Are you seriously not coming to work?

525
00:42:12,074 --> 00:42:15,360
If you keep doing this, I'll sue you
for breach of your employment contract

526
00:42:15,360 --> 00:42:18,497
and make sure no other firm hires you.

527
00:42:18,497 --> 00:42:21,190
Breach of my employment contract?

528
00:42:21,190 --> 00:42:24,253
I've asked you for years to give me
a written contract, but you never did.

529
00:42:24,253 --> 00:42:27,120
Hey, Kang! Have you lost your mind?

530
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:43,865
Hello, Attorney Kim Sang Chun,
head of CHUNJEONG Law Firm.

531
00:42:43,865 --> 00:42:47,465
- This is Cha Eun Kyung.
- How did she even get his name?

532
00:42:47,465 --> 00:42:49,358
Article 17 of the Labor Standards Act.

533
00:42:49,358 --> 00:42:54,236
You know that not providing a written contract
is a criminal offense, right?

534
00:42:54,236 --> 00:42:57,474
How can you still not use
written employment contracts these days?

535
00:42:57,474 --> 00:43:00,675
And stop calling Attorney Kang "hey."

536
00:43:00,675 --> 00:43:03,417
Isn't that a breach of an attorney's duty
to maintain dignity?

537
00:43:03,417 --> 00:43:09,140
Who are you to tell me what to do?
Are you her boss already?

538
00:43:09,140 --> 00:43:13,420
Well, I'm just her senior lawyer.

539
00:43:14,121 --> 00:43:15,714
For now.

540
00:43:19,755 --> 00:43:22,234
Hello? Hello!

541
00:43:23,437 --> 00:43:24,901
Unbelievable!

542
00:43:26,376 --> 00:43:29,321
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

543
00:43:29,321 --> 00:43:32,831
What brings you here? Did you come to see me?

544
00:43:32,831 --> 00:43:37,677
No... I came to meet Attorney Park.

545
00:43:37,677 --> 00:43:39,330
Park Tae Su again?

546
00:43:39,936 --> 00:43:42,824
Did I miss my chance?

547
00:43:44,043 --> 00:43:46,358
No. Not yet.

548
00:43:48,545 --> 00:43:53,351
We don't send our lawyers out
for consultations.

549
00:43:53,351 --> 00:43:55,428
And we don't pressure them to bring in clients.

550
00:43:56,091 --> 00:44:00,340
- How did you find all that out?
- I'm Cha Eun Kyung.

551
00:44:00,340 --> 00:44:01,740
I looked into everything.

552
00:44:04,094 --> 00:44:06,631
I've been waiting for you, Kang.

553
00:44:09,308 --> 00:44:14,050
Your passion and sincerity toward your clients.

554
00:44:14,050 --> 00:44:17,436
Those matter more in the divorce team
than in other departments.

555
00:44:18,200 --> 00:44:21,339
I think you'd make a great divorce lawyer.

556
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:25,534
Me? You really think so?

557
00:44:25,534 --> 00:44:27,041
Of course I do.

558
00:44:29,127 --> 00:44:34,658
Actually, there's something
I've wanted to ask you.

559
00:44:34,658 --> 00:44:38,593
Go ahead. I'm not opposing counsel anymore.

560
00:44:38,593 --> 00:44:44,072
In the Seo Ji Hoon and Park Na Yeon case,
Park said she didn't want a divorce back then.

561
00:44:44,072 --> 00:44:46,618
How did you convince your client?

562
00:44:47,771 --> 00:44:49,946
I showed her what was in store for her.

563
00:44:51,692 --> 00:44:54,471
If you want to learn those things,
come be my associate.

564
00:44:55,404 --> 00:44:59,361
So I can hire you now, Attorney Kang?

565
00:45:03,120 --> 00:45:05,720
Yes, if the offer still stands.

566
00:45:19,900 --> 00:45:21,646
I'm home.

567
00:45:21,646 --> 00:45:23,640
Hey, sweetheart. You're home!

568
00:45:29,766 --> 00:45:31,166
Dad.

569
00:45:32,024 --> 00:45:33,424
I...

570
00:45:34,318 --> 00:45:36,696
I'm thinking of moving to a firm in Seoul.

571
00:45:36,696 --> 00:45:38,096
Really?

572
00:45:39,198 --> 00:45:43,834
Wow! That's great! What made you decide?

573
00:45:43,834 --> 00:45:46,125
I met someone I want to learn from.

574
00:45:49,340 --> 00:45:51,740
So, here's the thing...

575
00:45:54,794 --> 00:45:56,554
You want me to come with you?

576
00:45:59,218 --> 00:46:04,035
I don't want to hold you back anymore.

577
00:46:04,035 --> 00:46:06,012
I can walk on my own now.

578
00:46:06,012 --> 00:46:09,657
So don't worry and go live your own life.

579
00:46:09,657 --> 00:46:11,445
Hold me back?

580
00:46:11,445 --> 00:46:14,877
You spent your whole life for me.
Why are you telling me to live my own life now?

581
00:46:15,859 --> 00:46:20,580
Can't you just do what I ask, just this once?

582
00:46:45,893 --> 00:46:48,248
[Seven years ago]
Mom, please!

583
00:46:48,248 --> 00:46:54,054
I should never have married your father.
And I shouldn't have had you.

584
00:47:31,552 --> 00:47:33,338
Dad, don't worry.

585
00:47:35,397 --> 00:47:36,797
I'll...

586
00:47:38,437 --> 00:47:41,820
I'll pass the bar exam. I promise.

587
00:47:41,820 --> 00:47:45,524
- We'll make it, all right?
- Okay.

588
00:47:47,304 --> 00:47:52,597
I'll do anything for you, too, Hye Seong.

589
00:47:52,597 --> 00:47:53,997
I'm sorry.

590
00:48:05,761 --> 00:48:08,615
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

591
00:48:16,007 --> 00:48:20,087
Dad, you must be sick of hospital food.
I'll make you something nice. What do you want?

592
00:48:20,943 --> 00:48:23,450
- Kimchi stew.
- Kimchi stew? Okay.

593
00:48:39,598 --> 00:48:43,446
All right.
We'll look for another attorney then.

594
00:49:07,355 --> 00:49:09,126
He's so stubborn.

595
00:49:09,126 --> 00:49:13,057
[Hyeseong's Bunsik]

596
00:49:17,791 --> 00:49:21,246
[Thank you for supporting
Hyeseong's Bunsik over the years.]

597
00:49:29,763 --> 00:49:33,406
Hey, Dad. What's that?

598
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:40,063
I thought maybe Hyeseong's Bunsik could move
to Seoul with its owner.

599
00:49:42,104 --> 00:49:47,086
Dad, you're not holding me back.
You're my whole world. You know that?

600
00:49:47,086 --> 00:49:48,861
Don't ever say that again.

601
00:49:48,861 --> 00:49:52,964
If you left me here in Gwangjin,
you'd keep thinking about me, right?

602
00:49:52,964 --> 00:49:55,594
Of course! I'd think about you every day!

603
00:49:57,097 --> 00:50:01,478
That's what holding you back means.
I'd be making you worry about me.

604
00:50:02,092 --> 00:50:05,567
So I've decided. I'm going with you.

605
00:50:07,465 --> 00:50:09,468
Thanks, Dad.

606
00:50:09,468 --> 00:50:10,868
You don't have to thank me.

607
00:50:12,095 --> 00:50:14,135
- Is this all?
- Yeah.

608
00:50:20,020 --> 00:50:23,412
Make sure you leave the house. It's dangerous.

609
00:50:44,586 --> 00:50:47,218
What are you doing here?

610
00:50:56,849 --> 00:51:00,089
Min Kyung! You...

611
00:51:48,130 --> 00:51:50,633
I'm terrified.

612
00:51:51,949 --> 00:51:55,532
I don't care about the two billion won.
I can't do this anymore.

613
00:51:55,532 --> 00:51:57,446
I'm calling the police right now.

614
00:51:57,446 --> 00:51:59,012
Wait.

615
00:51:59,012 --> 00:52:00,412
Just a moment.

616
00:52:05,584 --> 00:52:09,151
Let's try this one last time.
We can still call the police afterward.

617
00:52:11,089 --> 00:52:13,179
[Complaint: Kim Min Kyung and
Ma Jeong Jin shall be divorced]

618
00:52:16,008 --> 00:52:17,189
[Defendant's Drug Use and Coercion of Others]

619
00:52:17,189 --> 00:52:18,263
[Video Stills of the Defendant Using Drugs]

620
00:52:18,263 --> 00:52:19,289
[Defendant's Drugs and Syringes]

621
00:52:22,222 --> 00:52:26,562
You said we had to keep this confidential.
Why did you write up a complaint?

622
00:52:26,562 --> 00:52:30,761
There's no rule saying
a complaint can only be filed with the court.

623
00:52:30,761 --> 00:52:34,461
There's nothing to hear! Let's go to trial!

624
00:52:37,334 --> 00:52:38,418
[Defendant's table]

625
00:52:38,418 --> 00:52:42,208
Since his lawyer isn't helping us reach
a settlement, let's send it directly to him.

626
00:52:45,832 --> 00:52:48,059
Stay at a hotel for just three days.

627
00:52:49,078 --> 00:52:53,293
You called me this late because
you had nowhere else to go, right?

628
00:52:57,606 --> 00:52:59,750
Oh, I can't accept this.

629
00:53:03,593 --> 00:53:06,580
I'll deduct it from the success fee later.

630
00:53:06,580 --> 00:53:12,446
Go enjoy a little staycation.
Swim, have a nice breakfast.

631
00:53:13,232 --> 00:53:16,373
All the things you missed out on
while spending five years cleaning the house.

632
00:53:19,071 --> 00:53:22,186
And if he calls, don't answer.

633
00:53:22,186 --> 00:53:25,354
It's his turn to live in fear now.

634
00:53:26,150 --> 00:53:29,885
We're close to reaching a settlement.

635
00:53:49,351 --> 00:53:53,670
[Complaint: Kim Min Kyung and
Ma Jeong Jin shall be divorced]

636
00:53:55,652 --> 00:53:57,052
What's this?

637
00:53:58,740 --> 00:54:01,344
Oh, come on. What a joke.

638
00:54:28,370 --> 00:54:30,630
Beautiful.

639
00:54:32,242 --> 00:54:37,367
I forgot how beautiful this city is at night.

640
00:54:59,419 --> 00:55:00,711
[Ma Jeong Jin]
Hey, did you go file a complaint?

641
00:55:00,711 --> 00:55:03,792
Don't even think about it!
Are you saying you won't settle?

642
00:55:03,792 --> 00:55:04,883
We need to talk.

643
00:55:04,883 --> 00:55:07,811
Why aren't you answering my calls?
You think I'm kidding?

644
00:55:33,834 --> 00:55:34,897
[REBOM Law Firm]

645
00:55:42,040 --> 00:55:43,045
[TAESU Law Firm]

646
00:55:50,612 --> 00:55:52,894
I'm sorry, Attorney Park.

647
00:55:55,159 --> 00:55:59,651
Don't be. Congratulations. I'll see you around.

648
00:55:59,651 --> 00:56:01,251
Okay.

649
00:56:14,254 --> 00:56:15,654
Come this way.

650
00:56:25,190 --> 00:56:28,876
[Korea Legal Culture Foundation Award
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung]

651
00:56:37,056 --> 00:56:39,608
[Power Woman of the Year
Cha Eun Kyung]

652
00:56:48,947 --> 00:56:53,686
You'll join me for three consultations
and court appearances a week.

653
00:56:53,686 --> 00:56:54,901
Is that okay?

654
00:56:54,901 --> 00:56:57,097
Yes! That sounds great!

655
00:56:57,097 --> 00:57:00,304
I've never had that opportunity at my old firm.

656
00:57:02,972 --> 00:57:06,592
It's just orientation today,
so take a look around and get settled.

657
00:57:06,592 --> 00:57:09,338
I'll give you your first assignments
on your first official day.

658
00:57:10,445 --> 00:57:11,845
Yes.

659
00:57:12,912 --> 00:57:18,490
Could I look through some case files first?

660
00:57:19,643 --> 00:57:23,293
I don't have much experience with
divorce cases, so I'd like to read up on them.

661
00:57:24,570 --> 00:57:25,970
Sure.

662
00:57:26,561 --> 00:57:28,381
[Senior Partner Cha Eun Kyung]

663
00:57:31,535 --> 00:57:32,742
Here you go.

664
00:57:32,742 --> 00:57:34,237
Thank you.

665
00:57:40,544 --> 00:57:44,001
Is this... drugs?

666
00:57:44,001 --> 00:57:46,289
Have you never seen a drug case before?

667
00:57:46,289 --> 00:57:49,011
No. This is my first one!

668
00:57:49,011 --> 00:57:50,179
Is it a criminal case?

669
00:57:50,179 --> 00:57:52,640
No, it's the other party in the divorce case.

670
00:57:52,640 --> 00:57:57,020
We've already made a deal that
we won't report him for now.

671
00:57:57,869 --> 00:58:00,265
That's definitely worth using in the
negotiation.

672
00:58:00,265 --> 00:58:03,503
If we report his drug use,
he'll be in serious trouble.

673
00:58:03,503 --> 00:58:05,031
He'd certainly be arrested.

674
00:58:05,031 --> 00:58:09,804
And everyone involved would be prosecuted.
So the others would blame him, too.

675
00:58:11,022 --> 00:58:13,800
You seem to know a lot about criminal cases.

676
00:58:13,800 --> 00:58:15,325
Exactly.

677
00:58:15,325 --> 00:58:19,458
I'm waiting for the fear of being reported to
make him pay two billion won.

678
00:58:19,458 --> 00:58:21,427
Two billion won?

679
00:58:22,044 --> 00:58:23,583
Is that even possible?

680
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:25,162
Why not?

681
00:58:25,162 --> 00:58:27,412
That's the price of keeping him out of prison.

682
00:58:28,633 --> 00:58:30,319
Like I told you,

683
00:58:30,319 --> 00:58:34,584
you have to chase down
every little lead in a divorce case.

684
00:58:40,684 --> 00:58:44,607
You're not like the others.

685
00:58:44,607 --> 00:58:45,640
Me?

686
00:58:45,640 --> 00:58:49,034
"We should report drug offenders
in the public interest."

687
00:58:49,034 --> 00:58:53,029
"We should put society's interests
ahead of our own."

688
00:58:53,029 --> 00:58:55,118
You don't say things like that.

689
00:58:55,118 --> 00:58:57,079
I've been a lawyer for five years.

690
00:58:57,079 --> 00:59:02,338
I've learned to separate my role as a lawyer
from my personal morals.

691
00:59:03,665 --> 00:59:07,998
Personally, I'd like to file criminal
complaints for assault and drug use right away.

692
00:59:12,065 --> 00:59:14,067
Speaking of that...

693
00:59:14,067 --> 00:59:17,068
Do you remember the difference
between a complaint and a report?

694
00:59:17,068 --> 00:59:19,299
You learned that in law school.

695
00:59:19,299 --> 00:59:22,007
Yes. A complaint is filed by the victim,

696
00:59:22,007 --> 00:59:27,212
while a report can be filed by a third party.

697
00:59:27,212 --> 00:59:28,804
Why are you asking me?

698
00:59:28,804 --> 00:59:31,482
Just testing your memory.

699
00:59:33,417 --> 00:59:34,817
Yes.

700
00:59:35,898 --> 00:59:40,232
Attorney Cha, Ms. Kim's husband is calling.
Should I put him through?

701
00:59:41,828 --> 00:59:44,560
Let's make him sweat a little.

702
00:59:44,560 --> 00:59:47,347
Tell him I'm in court and will call back.

703
00:59:47,347 --> 00:59:48,747
Yes.

704
01:00:12,714 --> 01:00:15,134
- Hello.
- The apartment is now in her name.

705
01:00:15,134 --> 01:00:19,642
I still can't believe you gave away two
billion won. I've never seen anything like it.

706
01:00:19,642 --> 01:00:23,453
It's better than going to prison!

707
01:00:25,004 --> 01:00:26,791
What the...

708
01:00:30,130 --> 01:00:32,778
Kim Min Kyung... You thief!

709
01:00:52,110 --> 01:00:53,828
Are you Ma Jeong Jin?

710
01:00:56,026 --> 01:00:57,426
Yes, I am.

711
01:01:02,079 --> 01:01:05,290
- You're under arrest on drug charges.
- Let go!

712
01:01:05,290 --> 01:01:07,125
Don't move!

713
01:01:07,125 --> 01:01:09,920
You have the right to an attorney
and the right to remain silent.

714
01:01:09,920 --> 01:01:13,547
Anything you say can be used
against you in court.

715
01:01:19,208 --> 01:01:20,608
Hello?

716
01:01:21,328 --> 01:01:23,517
Did Ma Jeong Jin get arrested by the police?

717
01:01:23,517 --> 01:01:27,701
Yes. The police called me. Was it you?

718
01:01:27,701 --> 01:01:31,525
No. A deal is a deal.

719
01:01:33,360 --> 01:01:36,234
He must have a lot of enemies.

720
01:01:36,234 --> 01:01:39,519
His drug buddies turned on him.

721
01:01:39,519 --> 01:01:41,265
What goes around comes around.

722
01:01:42,319 --> 01:01:46,842
Ms. Kim, you can go home now.

723
01:01:46,842 --> 01:01:49,290
Back to your safe home.

724
01:01:51,629 --> 01:01:53,916
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

725
01:01:54,812 --> 01:01:56,612
Thank you so much.

726
01:02:02,387 --> 01:02:06,506
Do you remember the difference
between a complaint and a report?

727
01:02:06,506 --> 01:02:09,237
Yes. A complaint is filed by the victim,

728
01:02:09,237 --> 01:02:14,397
while a report can be filed by a third party.

729
01:02:14,397 --> 01:02:16,093
Why are you asking me?

730
01:02:16,093 --> 01:02:17,696
Just testing your memory.

731
01:02:17,696 --> 01:02:20,022
She got what I was getting at?

732
01:02:25,700 --> 01:02:26,750
Yes, Ma'am.

733
01:02:26,750 --> 01:02:29,412
Ma Jeong Jin has been arrested.

734
01:02:29,412 --> 01:02:31,931
Oh, really?

735
01:02:31,931 --> 01:02:34,838
Looks like a third party reported him.

736
01:02:34,838 --> 01:02:39,881
I'll officially be part of REBOM
starting next week, as stated in my contract.

737
01:02:39,881 --> 01:02:41,314
So I'm still a third party for now!

738
01:02:41,314 --> 01:02:43,794
How did you figure that out so quickly?

739
01:02:44,823 --> 01:02:46,478
You can tell you're experienced.

740
01:02:47,226 --> 01:02:49,853
I've already learned so much on my first day!

741
01:02:49,853 --> 01:02:51,104
Good work.

742
01:02:51,104 --> 01:02:52,213
Thank you.

743
01:02:57,653 --> 01:02:59,152
Can I...

744
01:03:00,638 --> 01:03:04,438
ask why you chose REBOM?

745
01:03:08,012 --> 01:03:12,437
I'm actually really into divorce cases.

746
01:03:12,437 --> 01:03:17,214
My dream is to become a registered
divorce specialist, just like you.

747
01:03:17,214 --> 01:03:18,813
I see.

748
01:03:19,726 --> 01:03:21,644
I was worried for nothing.

749
01:03:23,226 --> 01:03:26,668
You'll learn all about divorce cases at REBOM.

750
01:03:26,668 --> 01:03:27,798
Get ready.

751
01:03:28,856 --> 01:03:30,256
I will!

752
01:03:36,289 --> 01:03:39,512
Get home safe.

753
01:03:39,512 --> 01:03:41,312
- Take care.
- You too.

754
01:03:45,379 --> 01:03:46,779
Hye Seong!

755
01:04:06,615 --> 01:04:12,287
Wow, look at you! Looking pretty good in Seoul.

756
01:04:15,022 --> 01:04:17,737
And you got a job at such a fancy firm.

757
01:04:26,621 --> 01:04:30,262
Can I ask why you chose REBOM?

758
01:04:35,834 --> 01:04:37,829
If I team up with you,

759
01:04:40,283 --> 01:04:43,538
I think I can get this woman
out of my dad's life.

760
01:05:36,240 --> 01:05:39,106
How did you find out about
your husband's affair?

761
01:05:39,106 --> 01:05:41,153
I guess it wasn't just physical.
He had feelings for her, too.

762
01:05:41,153 --> 01:05:43,477
That upsets me.
I don't want to hire your firm anymore!

763
01:05:43,477 --> 01:05:45,845
If I feature the person
everyone's talking about right on my channel,

764
01:05:45,845 --> 01:05:48,323
the algorithm will pick it up,
and my subscribers will double!

765
01:05:48,323 --> 01:05:53,558
Attorney Kang, you'll have to let go of
a lot of your old ways.
